<PolicyLayout
  title="AI Ads Lab Privacy Policy"
  description="How AI Ads Lab, operated by HMFIC Marketing LLC, accesses, uses, stores, and deletes data from members' Meta ad accounts."
  path="/ai-ads-lab/privacy"
  updated="October 21, 2026"
>
  <h2>About AI Ads Lab</h2>
  <p>
    AI Ads Lab (the "Service") is operated by HMFIC Marketing LLC ("we", "us",
    "our"). It helps business owners and creators ("members") plan, build,
    launch, and report on advertising campaigns in their own Meta ad account.
    The Service connects to Meta through Meta's official Marketing API, using
    Facebook Login for Business.
  </p>

  <h2>What data we access</h2>
  <p>When a member connects their Meta account, the Service may access:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Basic profile information Meta returns at login (name and Facebook user ID).</li>
    <li>The list of ad accounts, Pages, and business portfolios the member chooses to share with the Service during login.</li>
    <li>For the <strong>one ad account the member selects</strong>: campaigns, ad sets, ads, creatives, audiences, pixel and conversion settings, and performance results (such as spend, impressions, clicks, leads, and purchases).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The Service works only inside the single ad account the member selects in
    our portal. It does not read or change any other ad account the member's
    login can reach. It does not access the member's password, private messages,
    personal Facebook posts, friends list, or payment methods on file with Meta.
  </p>
  <p>
    We also store what members give us directly: their name, email address,
    answers to our onboarding questions (business, offer, audience, and brand
    voice), and any images or videos they upload for their ads. Subscription
    payments are processed by Stripe; we never see or store full card numbers.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use the data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To write ad plans, ad copy, scripts, and images for the member's business.</li>
    <li>To build campaigns in the member's ad account. Campaigns are created paused, and nothing goes live or spends money until the member approves it.</li>
    <li>To pull performance results and prepare the member's reports and recommendations.</li>
    <li>To provide support and run the member's account with us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use a member's ad account data to advertise to that member, to
    build audiences for anyone else, or to train AI models. We do not sell
    member data.
  </p>

  <h2>Data storage and security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is stored in a private database operated on our behalf by our hosting
    providers. Meta access tokens are encrypted at rest. Access is limited to
    the member and to the HMFIC Marketing LLC personnel operating the Service.
    Meta access tokens expire after about 60 days unless the member reconnects.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or trade member data. We share it only with the
    service providers that run the Service for us, under confidentiality
    obligations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Anthropic (Claude API), to generate ad plans, copy, and analysis.</li>
    <li>Supabase and Vercel, to host the database and member portal.</li>
    <li>Stripe, to process subscription payments.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data if the law requires it, or to protect the rights,
    safety, or property of our members, ourselves, or others.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep member data while the member's account is active. When a member
    cancels or asks us to delete their data, we delete it within 30 days, except
    for records we must keep by law (such as billing records).
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and deletion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can disconnect AI Ads Lab at any time from <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings/?tab=business_tools">Facebook Settings → Business Integrations</a>. This immediately stops our access to your Meta account.</li>
    <li>You can ask us to delete all of your data. See our <a href="/ai-ads-lab/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> page for the steps.</li>
    <li>You can ask for a copy of the data we hold about you, or ask us to correct it, by emailing us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is for businesses and is not directed to anyone under 18. We do
    not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. We will tell members about material changes
    before they take effect. The date at the top of this page shows the latest
    version.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
